### Page 3 of 3

```text
Planning and Development Department
2101 O’NeH Avenue, Suite 202, Cheyenne WY 82001
(Phone) 307-637-6282 (Fax) 307-637-6366
1vrnNIrY
II
STAFF MEMO
Re: Adoption of 2017 National Electrical Code
From: Robert Briggs, AICP, Director of Planning and Development
To: Mayor and City Council
Date: April 4, 2018
Recommendation:
Staff recommends adoption of the attached ordinance.
Background:
The state of Wyoming routinely adopts new editions of the National Electrical Code (NEC), International
Fire Code (IFC), the International Building Code (IBC), the International Mechanical Code (IMC), the
International Existing Building Code (IEBC) and the International Fuel Gas Code (IFGC) as the life safety
standards for construction in the state of Wyoming. In order for a Wyoming community to exert home
rule for inspection of commercial structures, the community must adopt the same versions of the NEC
and International Codes that have been adopted by the State Council on Fire Prevention and Electrical
Safety in Buildings (W.S. §35-9-121).
This means that the City of Cheyenne must routinely adopt new versions of the National Electrical Code
and International Codes as they become available and are adopted by the state. The ordinance before
the Council amends the existing Title 15 of the Cheyenne Municipal Code in the following ways:
•
Adopts the 2017 National Electrical Code to supersede the previously adopted 2014 code.
•
Changes the language for a local amendment to the NEC regarding the location of shut off
equipment to standard language used in industry and code. (The reason for this local
amendment is to place the location of the shut-offfor electrical service in a standard location,
making it easier to find in the event of afire, orfor convenience and safety of the building
owner).
•
Eliminates a redundant provision regarding the use of certain cable in residential construction.
Provisions for the use of this cable are already contained within the NEC, and the NEC governs
all electrical work within the city.
END OF MEMO
```
